---
title: "Creature creator"
note: "A creature for Krea 2: one of seventy kinds (dragons, griffins, krakens, hydras, owlbears, kitsune, sand worms, kaiju, mimics, wendigos, jellyfish titans, axolotl drakes …), each with its own shape and size, a covering that fits its skin (scales, feathers, fur, slime, chitin, hide, stone, bark, shadow) in the signature colour, and one or two features you remember. Its habitat follows its home, a forest, a sea, a cave, a volcano, the sky. It keeps what the picture cannot show (EXPORT:): its temperament, what it eats and the sound it makes, so a reel that casts it from the gallery reads $beast.call for its SFX. One seed is one creature, from four sides by the grid; $backdrop puts it in its habitat instead of the studio, $view one side only to try creatures faster."
tags: [krea, creatures, references]
---
$colour = __characters/creator/colour__
$kind = __characters/creatures/kind__
$size = $kind.size
$age = {young:2|full-grown:4|ancient:2}
$covering = __characters/creatures/covering[skin=$kind.skin]__
$features = {1-2$$__characters/creatures/feature__}
$home = __characters/creatures/habitat[home=$kind.home]__
$backdrop = {studio:3|habitat:2}
$who = $kind, $size and $age, with $kind.shape, covered in $covering, with $features
# What the picture carries beyond its prompt (EXPORT:): a screenplay that casts it reads $beast.temper, $beast.call …
EXPORT:
  who = $who
  $kind
  size = $size
  age = $age
  home = $home
  $colour
  temper = __characters/creatures/nature[aspect=temper]__
  diet = __characters/creatures/nature[aspect=diet]__
  call = __characters/creatures/nature[aspect=call]__
# The grid runs every view: one creature from four sides. Set $view to one of them to try creatures faster.
# The shot comes first, before the creature, and the view's sentence after it.
$look = {photo:4|animated:2|painted:2|concept:2}
$view = {head|three-quarter|side|front}
$opening = {IF $look is photo: A photograph of a lifelike practical creature, as on a film set|{IF $look is animated: A 3D creature render, in the style of a modern animated feature film|{IF $look is painted: A naturalist's watercolour plate|A creature concept-art painting}}}
$shot = {IF $view is head: a close-up of the head and neck alone, filling the frame,|{IF $view is three-quarter: a three-quarter view of the whole creature|{IF $view is side: a full side view of the whole body, from the head to the tip of the tail,|a front view of the whole creature}}}
$pose = {IF $view is head: Only the head and neck are in frame.|{IF $view is three-quarter: It is turned three-quarters to the left.|{IF $view is side: It stands side-on, with space around it in frame.|It faces the camera.}}}
$finish = {IF $look is photo: Shot on a 50mm lens, true colours, every scale and hair sharp.|{IF $look is animated: Stylised shapes, soft subsurface light.|{IF $look is painted: Fine ink lines and translucent washes on cream paper.|Loose painterly strokes and a clear silhouette.}}}
$opening: $shot of $who. $pose Behind it is {IF $backdrop is studio: a seamless mid-grey studio backdrop|$home, softly out of focus}, in soft, even light. $finish
@size 1216x832
@grid $view
